    {
      "id": "964ba456-b00f-4eb4-9c59-141003f930c0",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Create SEO WordPress blog drafts with Gemini and Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a weekly schedule, pulls the next pending blog topic from Google Sheets, and checks WordPress to avoid creating duplicate drafts. If no existing post is found, it uses Gemini to generate SEO article HTML and image briefs, creates three images, uploads them to WordPress, builds the final article, and saves it as a WordPress draft. It then updates the source sheet and sends Gmail notifications for either reconciled existing posts or newly created drafts.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the weekly schedule trigger for the desired publishing cadence.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the spreadsheet, sheet, status fields, and row identifiers used for the blog queue.\n- Configure WordPress credentials or REST API authentication for post lookup, category lookup, media upload, draft creation, and metadata updates.\n- Connect Google Gemini credentials for both article generation and image/image-brief generation nodes.\n- Connect Gmail credentials and set the notification recipients, subject lines, and message content.\n- Replace placeholder WordPress REST API URLs and verify slug, category, featured image, excerpt, and draft-status mappings.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Google Sheet columns, Gemini prompts, article validation rules, image count or style, WordPress category logic, and notification templates to match the site’s editorial workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
